<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0"><head><title>Playing Maze Rats in Pointliner</title></head><body>
<outline text="# Playing Maze Rats in Pointliner">
  <outline text="Maze Rats wired into Pointliner: stats, 2d6 saves, and above all its random tables, all live pills. Maze Rats is almost all tables, so it is one of the best Pointliner fits here. See maze-rats.md for the walkthrough. The dice, stat and table pills are complete; the tables carry filler options you replace with the book's own entries. Every pill here is live, click one to run it."/>
  <outline text="Adapted from Maze Rats by Ben Milton, used under CC BY 4.0 (creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0). Changes made: the tables and procedures are restructured into outline points and pills. Maze Rats is named descriptively; no logo or art is reproduced.">
    <outline text="The tables below hold filler options written for this demo, not the book's own entries. Replace the filler inside each `{rule ...}` with the entries from your copy; every pill is already wired, so a table updates the moment you edit its rule."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## A character in one roll">
    <outline text="Roll your stats from one pool and note the modifiers, then set them as variables so saves read them."/>
    <outline text="Roll your stats: {6d6}"/>
    <outline text="Health, rolled once: {1d6}"/>
    <outline text="Health, the number you track: {hp := 4}"/>
    <outline text="Set your final ability modifiers: {str := 1}, {dex := 0}, {wil := 2}."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Saves">
    <outline text="Risk is a 2d6 roll plus an ability modifier against a target. Change a modifier above and every save that reads it updates.">
      <outline text="Strength save: {2d6} + {str} (beat the target for the task)"/>
      <outline text="Dexterity save: {2d6} + {dex}"/>
      <outline text="Will save: {2d6} + {wil}"/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## The tables">
    <outline text="Each table is a weighted pick, one click for a result. Declare one with the rule keyword, as `{rule name: option | option}`, then call it by name anywhere. A bare `name: option | option` is ordinary text and registers nothing. Replace the filler options with the book's entries, separated by bars."/>
    <outline text="{rule monster: goblin | skeleton | giant rat | cave lurker | bandit}"/>
    <outline text="{rule room: empty | a trap | old bones | a locked chest | running water}"/>
    <outline text="Roll the room: {room}. What is in it: a {monster} guarding it."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Improvised spells (the signature trick)">
    <outline text="Maze Rats builds spells by combining two word-lists. That is a rule that calls two others, so one click gives a fresh spell every time. Replace the filler words with the book's form and effect lists."/>
    <outline text="{rule spell_form: bolt | cloud | ward | veil | swarm}"/>
    <outline text="{rule spell_effect: of fire | of silence | of thorns | of the void | of mending}"/>
    <outline text="{rule spell: a {spell_form} {spell_effect}}"/>
    <outline text="Cast something improvised: {spell}. Click it again for a new one."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Combat, fast">
    <outline text="Roll to hit, roll damage, edit health down. No spreadsheet, just dice and one variable.">
      <outline text="Attack: {2d6} + {str}   Damage: {1d6}"/>
      <outline text="Health: edit the hp variable down as you take hits. The {1d6} above is only the roll that set it; clicking a dice pill re-rolls it, so the variable is what holds the value."/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Run it yourself">
    <outline text="Roll {6d6} for stats and {1d6} for health, then set the modifier variables. Roll {2d6} plus a modifier for a save. Click a table pill for a monster or room, and click {spell} for an improvised spell. Roll to hit and roll damage in a fight. Swap the filler for the book's own tables and it becomes a pocket generator for a whole dungeon."/>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body></opml>
